# Red Panda website — public configuration.
#
# Every value here is inlined into the client bundle at build time and is
# permanently public. NO SECRET MAY EVER BE PUT IN A NEXT_PUBLIC_* VARIABLE:
# not an API key, not an AdMob credential, not a Google OAuth client secret,
# not a database URL. This website talks to no backend and needs none of them.
#
# All three values are OPTIONAL. The site builds and serves correctly with the
# file absent entirely — each surface renders an honest "not available yet"
# state instead of a broken link. Copy this file to `.env.local` for local work,
# or set the variables in your hosting provider's build settings.

# The public origin this site is served from, with no trailing slash.
# Used for canonical URLs, Open Graph, robots.txt and sitemap.xml.
# Must be an absolute https origin. When unset, no canonical or sitemap entries
# are emitted and every page is marked noindex — a preview build must not
# compete with the real site in a search index.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# The published support mailbox.
# Load-bearing, not decorative: an account created with Google or WhatsApp has
# no password and therefore no in-app deletion path, so this address is the ONLY
# route to account deletion for those users. Until it is set, /support and
# /delete-account say so plainly rather than showing an address nobody reads.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPPORT_EMAIL=

# The Google Play listing, once it exists.
# Accepted only when the host is play.google.com — an arbitrary URL here would
# put a store call-to-action in front of visitors that leads somewhere else.
# While unset, the homepage shows a non-clickable "Coming to Google Play"
# status. Leave it empty until the listing is live.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_PLAY_URL=
